        "review_body": "Good afternoon,\n\nI recently received the pearl earrings I ordered for my daughter. To ensure I had made a good purchase, I took them to a respected family-owned jeweler in Bethesda, Maryland, that has been in business for more than 70 years.\n\nAfter examining the earrings, they shared that while the pearls were of acceptable quality, they were not exceptional. They also noted that the pearls appeared to be approximately 8mm, even though I specifically requested the larger size within the advertised range (8.5mm).\n\nWhen I asked about value, they estimated that, without the branding, packaging, marketing, and online presence, the earrings would likely retail in the $350–$400 range. I even considered purchasing a pair from them and returning yours. However, the jeweler candidly advised that the time and effort involved in making the return likely would not be worth the difference. I appreciated their honesty, particularly since it meant they did not make a sale.\n\nNeedless to say, I was disappointed to hear this assessment and equally disappointed with the product I received. I find it difficult to believe that no one has raised similar concerns in the past, although I understand I have no way of knowing.\n\nI wanted to share this feedback in the hope that you will review the quality and sizing of the pearls being sold, as the product I received did not meet the expectations created by your descriptions.",
